    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the roster as our premier play at an 83.29 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Singer, paired with a significant 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage and a high-leverage leadoff spot, makes him the engine of our lineup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.61) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.46) also offer high-floor production, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefiting substantially from the 14% SP Skill boost provided by the Mitch Keller matchup. **Heliot Ramos** remains a strong start (70.57) as his path to production is cleared by a hitter-friendly park and a favorable matchup against the lower-tier Feltner, maximizing his counting stat potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning involved **Nolan Schanuel** and his 54.68 score. While he presented a stable option against the lefty Jake Bennett, the optimizer opted for **Curtis Mead** (63.58) and **Nasim Nunez** (61.41) in the infield to capitalize on the weak SP_xERA of Mitch Keller. **Nolan Schanuel** fell just outside the threshold for daily game caps, though his proximity to the starting lineup keeps him as our primary pivot if any of our starters are scratched upon official lineup confirmation. Conversely, we are closely monitoring the 38% rain risk surrounding **Brayan Rocchio**; while his 58.86 score justifies the start, he remains the most volatile asset in our utility slot should weather conditions shift closer to first pitch.\n\nBeyond the rain risk for **Brayan Rocchio**, managers should be wary of the matchup for **Jackson Merrill** (53.12). Facing Shohei Ohtani represents our most difficult test of the day, as the SP_xERA of 3.37 significantly suppresses his base projection despite his favorable platoon split. While **Andy Pages** (65.92) and **Drake Baldwin** (59.13) provide solid secondary support, we are tracking their batting orders closely; any move away from the top two spots in the lineup would trigger a re-evaluation of their daily value, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** who relies on that leadoff designation to sustain his current scoring tier.",
